{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123458","id":4516725690,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDTfDug","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123458.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123458/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123458/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123458/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/172eb952d55a5e536f9772f1c2ea5df58a07565c","number":123458,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix hundreds of missing Oxford commas","user":{"login":"JimmyCushnie","id":32693298,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjkzMjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32693298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie","html_url":"https://github.com/JimmyCushnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JimmyCushnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While doing #123456 (which this PR is built on) for the meme, I noticed that there are actually a LOT of missing commas in the docs.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nOur [writing guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/documentation/guidelines/docs_writing_guidelines.html) for class documentation state to \"always [...] use the Oxford comma\". This rule is currently broken in hundreds of places across the docs. This PR fixes every instance of a missing Oxford comma that I could find.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI assume that this guideline is up to date and agreed upon in spite of its widespread violation. I searched RocketChat to see if there was any previous discussion of this, but all I could find was a comment from @Mickeon in 2024 which included it in a list of \"guidelines that still hold up and have shown to be net positives\".\r\n\r\nI personally strongly support the use of the Oxford comma in documentation. I think this PR improves the clarity of every sentence it touches.\r\n\r\nI proofread the diff twice to make sure I was only adding genuine Oxford commas and not hitting any false positives.\r\n\r\nIf the maintainers like this PR, I am interested in doing additional PRs to clean up other inconsistently-applied guidelines. (For example, \"however\" is supposed to be a banned word but currently appears 169 times in the class docs.)\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changes that aren't strictly comma additions\r\n\r\nWhile making this PR I noticed a few small issues with the docs that are not strictly missing commas, but which occur around missing commas. I decided to fix these with this PR, but I can remove them if it's better to limit the scope of this PR to only added commas.\r\n\r\nThe affected files are:\r\n\r\n* `ShaderMaterial.xml`\r\n* `SystemFont.xml`","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"